1
00:00:01,610 --> 00:00:03,264
- [Senu] It's nice to meet you!

2
00:00:05,222 --> 00:00:08,051
- The beastmen from
Howling Village moved here.

3
00:00:08,182 --> 00:00:10,923
If you need anything,
just ask Lamulias here.

4
00:00:11,054 --> 00:00:12,838
- It's very nice to meet you.

5
00:00:12,969 --> 00:00:14,231
- Yes!

6
00:00:14,362 --> 00:00:16,364
- You don't need
to be that formal.

7
00:00:16,494 --> 00:00:19,628
Apparently they all thought
that they were going to be

8
00:00:19,758 --> 00:00:22,022
treated horribly
when they moved here.

9
00:00:23,588 --> 00:00:26,504
Naturally, we have
no such intentions.

10
00:00:26,635 --> 00:00:30,682
- There appear to be no issues
with the new residents, but...

11
00:00:30,813 --> 00:00:31,596
- [Hiraku] But?

12
00:00:31,727 --> 00:00:32,858
[girls gasping]

13
00:00:32,989 --> 00:00:34,686
- [Lamulias] They faint
quite often.

14
00:00:34,817 --> 00:00:38,038
- [Hiraku] Well, they'll just
have to get used to things.

15
00:00:39,735 --> 00:00:42,912
["Flower Ring" by Shino Shimoji
and Aya Suzaki plays]

16
00:02:09,477 --> 00:02:11,435
[all laughing]

17
00:02:11,566 --> 00:02:12,697
- Wait!

18
00:02:12,828 --> 00:02:15,570
- Come and get us!

19
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:19,269
[magic whirring]
[boy gasping]

20
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:22,142
- Geez, you need to be
careful when you play.

21
00:02:22,272 --> 00:02:23,882
- You can use magic too, Senu?

22
00:02:24,013 --> 00:02:25,884
- Yes. Yes, I can.

23
00:02:26,015 --> 00:02:29,192
- Don't tell me Tia, am I the
only one who can't use magic?

24
00:02:29,323 --> 00:02:34,284
- Well, all of the angels
can use magic.

25
00:02:34,415 --> 00:02:37,418
- And all the high elves
can use magic.

26
00:02:37,548 --> 00:02:38,941
[water splashing]

27
00:02:39,071 --> 00:02:41,117
- It is common for us
to be able to use

28
00:02:41,248 --> 00:02:43,206
fire and water magic.

29
00:02:43,337 --> 00:02:45,513
- We're good with using
magic for water.

30
00:02:45,643 --> 00:02:48,820
[fire roaring]

31
00:02:48,951 --> 00:02:50,431
[Hiraku clapping]

32
00:02:50,561 --> 00:02:52,520
- Even the bees can do it.

33
00:02:54,391 --> 00:02:57,612
[fire roaring]

34
00:02:57,742 --> 00:02:59,179
- Don't worry, mayor!

35
00:02:59,309 --> 00:03:00,963
There are others with no magic.

36
00:03:01,093 --> 00:03:03,139
- Hey, let's practice
together, mayor.

37
00:03:03,270 --> 00:03:04,662
- Yeah, you're right.

38
00:03:04,793 --> 00:03:06,882
I have a feeling these
kids will surpass me.

39
00:03:07,012 --> 00:03:10,320
Oh well, there's no point in
wishing for the impossible.

40
00:03:10,451 --> 00:03:12,670
I'll just focus on
what I can do for now.

41
00:03:12,801 --> 00:03:15,760
[ground rumbling]

42
00:03:15,891 --> 00:03:17,762
What was That? An earthquake?

43
00:03:18,850 --> 00:03:20,200
- Mayor!

44
00:03:20,330 --> 00:03:21,853
A grappler bear
and a bloody viper

45
00:03:21,984 --> 00:03:23,507
are fighting in the forest!

46
00:03:23,638 --> 00:03:25,901
- Bear and viper.

47
00:03:26,031 --> 00:03:27,598
A bear and a snake?

48
00:03:27,729 --> 00:03:30,514
[ground rumbling]
[both grunting]

49
00:03:30,645 --> 00:03:33,822
Those two fighting each other is
enough to make the ground shake?

50
00:03:33,952 --> 00:03:35,563
- What should we do?

51
00:03:36,564 --> 00:03:38,130
- A bear and a viper.

52
00:03:38,261 --> 00:03:41,090
- If this continues,
it might affect the village,

53
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:44,049
but I fear it would be dangerous
to get involved without a plan.

54
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:45,747
- Yeah, that's true.

55
00:03:45,877 --> 00:03:48,837
So those animals, do you
think we can eat them?

56
00:03:48,967 --> 00:03:50,578
[Granmaria gasps]

57
00:03:51,796 --> 00:03:53,233
So anyways,

58
00:03:53,363 --> 00:03:56,018
I've heard that hunters
sometimes eat bear meat.

59
00:03:56,148 --> 00:03:58,629
I've always wondered how
bear meat would taste.

60
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:00,457
- Right.

61
00:04:00,588 --> 00:04:01,719
Down there. Look.

62
00:04:01,850 --> 00:04:03,721
[dramatic music]

63
00:04:03,852 --> 00:04:06,289
[beasts growling]

64
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:07,116
- [Hiraku] Whoa!

65
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:08,465
They're big.

66
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:11,033
- We should go back for help.

67
00:04:11,163 --> 00:04:13,340
- No, just take me down
really fast.

68
00:04:13,470 --> 00:04:14,863
[Granmaria gasps]

69
00:04:14,993 --> 00:04:17,169
- I understand.

70
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,432
[dramatic music continues]

71
00:04:18,562 --> 00:04:19,650
[Hiraku grunts]
[sword slicing]

72
00:04:19,781 --> 00:04:21,261
[ground rumbling]

73
00:04:23,175 --> 00:04:25,003
- Haven't had a big one
in a while.

74
00:04:25,134 --> 00:04:27,354
- [Lizardmen] One, two!

75
00:04:27,484 --> 00:04:28,485
- What's wrong?

76
00:04:28,616 --> 00:04:29,921
- You think you
could take down

77
00:04:30,052 --> 00:04:31,575
a monster like that
with one attack?

78
00:04:31,706 --> 00:04:32,707
- No way.

79
00:04:32,837 --> 00:04:34,012
- That's crazy.

80
00:04:34,143 --> 00:04:35,666
The mayor is something else.

81
00:04:35,797 --> 00:04:37,102
- Wow.

82
00:04:37,233 --> 00:04:39,757
Looking at him up close,
he really is huge.

83
00:04:39,888 --> 00:04:42,369
- As far as cooking
the bear goes,

84
00:04:42,499 --> 00:04:44,284
what do you plan to make?

85
00:04:44,414 --> 00:04:46,416
- Got an idea.

86
00:04:46,547 --> 00:04:48,113
[fire crackling]
[light music]

87
00:04:48,244 --> 00:04:51,116
I'll add some of these
herbs and spices.

88
00:04:51,247 --> 00:04:53,205
Now we add wine and simmer.

89
00:04:53,336 --> 00:04:54,859
- [Both] Our delicious,
precious wine?

90
00:04:54,990 --> 00:04:56,034
- [Hiraku] It's fine.

91
00:04:56,165 --> 00:04:58,385
That kind of cooking is normal.

92
00:04:58,515 --> 00:04:59,516
And there we have it;

93
00:04:59,647 --> 00:05:02,171
wine braised grappler bear.

94
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:03,955
[both gasping]

95
00:05:04,086 --> 00:05:05,435
[Hiraku chewing]

96
00:05:05,566 --> 00:05:07,437
It's incredibly gamey.

97
00:05:07,568 --> 00:05:08,917
- [Both] Our delicious,
precious wine.

98
00:05:09,047 --> 00:05:12,312
- I'm telling you,
this is normal.

99
00:05:12,442 --> 00:05:14,183
And this is the blood viper.

100
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:16,054
I tried frying it.

101
00:05:17,012 --> 00:05:18,230
[Hiraku humming]

102
00:05:18,361 --> 00:05:20,755
That tastes just like
fried chicken!

103
00:05:20,885 --> 00:05:22,278
- It's delicious!

104
00:05:22,409 --> 00:05:25,237
- It tastes different
than I thought.

105
00:05:25,368 --> 00:05:27,501
- [Hiraku] It tastes
surprisingly like
chicken breast,

106
00:05:27,631 --> 00:05:29,546
which means my plate
is missing something

107
00:05:29,677 --> 00:05:32,593
that goes right here.

108
00:05:32,723 --> 00:05:35,291
- So then, what brings
you here today?

109
00:05:35,422 --> 00:05:38,686
- Perhaps, do you have
an antibacterial agent?

110
00:05:38,816 --> 00:05:40,035
- Antibacterial?

111
00:05:40,165 --> 00:05:41,645
- Yeah.

112
00:05:41,776 --> 00:05:44,561
I need to use it for a new
recipe I want to try out.

113
00:05:44,692 --> 00:05:48,130
Do you have any medicines that
can kill harmful microorganisms?

114
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:49,740
- Microorganisms?

115
00:05:49,871 --> 00:05:51,873
Those are the things
you spoke of before!

116
00:05:52,003 --> 00:05:53,744
- Yeah, that's them.

117
00:05:53,875 --> 00:05:55,877
I want something that will
prevent stomach aches
or illness.

118
00:05:56,007 --> 00:05:57,008
- I see!

119
00:05:57,139 --> 00:05:58,880
Just leave it to me.

120
00:05:59,010 --> 00:06:01,361
How about this one here?

121
00:06:01,491 --> 00:06:05,016
One dose will blast anything to
the other side of the mountains.

122
00:06:05,147 --> 00:06:07,062
- [Hiraku] Do you have
anything more peaceful?

123
00:06:07,192 --> 00:06:08,933
- Then how about this one?

124
00:06:09,064 --> 00:06:11,501
This one is safe enough
to use in foods.

125
00:06:11,632 --> 00:06:13,242
- Yeah, this'll work.

126
00:06:13,373 --> 00:06:14,112
Thanks.

127
00:06:14,243 --> 00:06:15,679
- Of course.

128
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:17,986
- By the way, how's the
miso production coming?

129
00:06:18,116 --> 00:06:19,291
[Flora groans]

130
00:06:19,422 --> 00:06:21,206
- The honest truth is
not very well.

131
00:06:21,337 --> 00:06:24,035
I did everything exactly
like you told me to,

132
00:06:24,166 --> 00:06:27,909
but no matter how long I waited,
it never started to ferment.

133
00:06:29,911 --> 00:06:31,303
[loud explosion]

134
00:06:31,434 --> 00:06:34,045
I've had to rebuild
my hut three times.

135
00:06:34,176 --> 00:06:35,873
- That's not supposed to happen!

136
00:06:36,004 --> 00:06:38,093
Well, let's give it
another try then.

137
00:06:38,223 --> 00:06:40,487
- Really?

138
00:06:40,617 --> 00:06:42,532
I'll keep the explosives
to a minimum.

139
00:06:42,663 --> 00:06:44,055
- Please don't use any.

140
00:06:44,186 --> 00:06:46,057
[rooster crowing]

141
00:06:46,188 --> 00:06:48,190
[chickens clucking]

142
00:06:49,844 --> 00:06:51,759
Yes! Perfect!

143
00:06:52,455 --> 00:06:53,804
[egg cracking]

144
00:06:53,935 --> 00:06:56,894
First, we gently beat the eggs.

145
00:06:57,025 --> 00:07:00,289
Add salt and vinegar.

146
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,160
This vinegar is made
from apples.

147
00:07:02,291 --> 00:07:03,858
- That's also fermented, right?

148
00:07:03,988 --> 00:07:05,337
[Hiraku laughs]

149
00:07:05,468 --> 00:07:07,862
- Then we mix it as we
slowly add in the oil.

150
00:07:07,992 --> 00:07:09,603
And now we have mayonnaise.

151
00:07:09,733 --> 00:07:11,082
- Oh!

152
00:07:11,213 --> 00:07:14,172
- Now it's exactly like
having fried chicken.

153
00:07:14,303 --> 00:07:15,609
- Oh, wow!

154
00:07:15,739 --> 00:07:17,828
I could eat this by itself
without food.

155
00:07:17,959 --> 00:07:20,265
- Stop that right now!
It's terrible for your health!

156
00:07:20,396 --> 00:07:23,617
Now then, onto making miso.

157
00:07:23,747 --> 00:07:26,924
First, we start by simmering
the soybeans we soaked in water.

158
00:07:27,055 --> 00:07:28,535
Then we grind them.

159
00:07:28,665 --> 00:07:31,015
[Flora humming]

160
00:07:31,146 --> 00:07:32,582
[magic whirring]

161
00:07:32,713 --> 00:07:34,410
Moldy, moldy, moldy.

162
00:07:34,541 --> 00:07:36,934
I used the almighty farming tool
to help make the koji mold.

163
00:07:37,065 --> 00:07:38,893
You don't need to
write that down.

164
00:07:39,023 --> 00:07:42,113
We mixed the koji with
salt and form balls.

165
00:07:43,724 --> 00:07:45,682
Now we pack it into barrels.

166
00:07:45,813 --> 00:07:47,554
- Oh, I see.

167
00:07:47,684 --> 00:07:50,295
Mine didn't work because
I didn't say "moldy-mold."

168
00:07:50,426 --> 00:07:53,951
- [Hiraku] No, that's,
well, maybe.

169
00:07:54,082 --> 00:07:56,084
Now we just let it
age in the cellar.

170
00:07:56,214 --> 00:07:58,782
It'll take a few months,
so let's wait patiently.

171
00:07:58,913 --> 00:08:00,305
- [Flora] That long?

172
00:08:00,436 --> 00:08:02,003
- Yeah.

173
00:08:02,133 --> 00:08:04,266
But all that time will make
the flavors even more intense.

174
00:08:04,396 --> 00:08:06,747
- This requires perseverance
just like research.

175
00:08:06,877 --> 00:08:07,704
- Right!
- Ah!

176
00:08:07,835 --> 00:08:09,227
There you are.

177
00:08:09,358 --> 00:08:11,316
You've got visitors.

178
00:08:11,447 --> 00:08:12,840
- Visitors?

179
00:08:14,189 --> 00:08:15,930
The visitors were
a group of dwarves

180
00:08:16,060 --> 00:08:18,019
led by a man named Donovan.

181
00:08:18,149 --> 00:08:19,977
- We are elder dwarves.

182
00:08:20,108 --> 00:08:21,675
- [Hiraku] What's the
difference?

183
00:08:21,805 --> 00:08:23,938
- We've heard that you have
high quality alcohol

184
00:08:24,068 --> 00:08:26,462
in this village and we'd
like you to share some.

185
00:08:26,593 --> 00:08:27,855
- Do you mean our wine?

186
00:08:27,985 --> 00:08:29,639
I'd be happy to share some.

187
00:08:29,770 --> 00:08:32,381
- Mayor Hiraku, I'm afraid we
can't give it away for free.

188
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:33,208
- Huh?

189
00:08:33,338 --> 00:08:34,296
- She's right.

190
00:08:34,426 --> 00:08:35,776
Our wine is very valuable.

191
00:08:35,906 --> 00:08:38,169
- I know, but they're
our guests here.

192
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:40,607
- I'm sorry, but we
don't have any money.

193
00:08:40,737 --> 00:08:43,218
However, we do have technology.

194
00:08:43,348 --> 00:08:44,611
- Technology?

195
00:08:44,741 --> 00:08:46,134
- That's right.

196
00:08:46,264 --> 00:08:48,745
We've spent our lives
studying alcohol production

197
00:08:48,876 --> 00:08:50,834
and we've traveled
a long way to get here.

198
00:08:50,965 --> 00:08:53,402
You have some very fine
crops in this village.

199
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:56,405
We can help you turn them
into fine alcohol.

200
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:58,015
What do you think?

201
00:08:58,146 --> 00:08:59,495
Don't you want to drink some?

202
00:08:59,626 --> 00:09:01,497
[all gasping]

203
00:09:02,933 --> 00:09:04,369
- [Hiraku] Donovan and
his men got to work

204
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,502
on the alcohol right away.

205
00:09:07,590 --> 00:09:08,809
Distillation.

206
00:09:08,939 --> 00:09:11,289
I remember doing this
in science class.

207
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:13,030
[alcohol drips]

208
00:09:13,161 --> 00:09:14,075
- Here you go!

209
00:09:14,205 --> 00:09:15,511
This is corn whiskey.

210
00:09:15,642 --> 00:09:17,600
- It's crystal clear!

211
00:09:17,731 --> 00:09:20,560
- It'll get its color when
we age it in the barrels.

212
00:09:20,690 --> 00:09:22,518
- Oh, I see.

213
00:09:23,475 --> 00:09:24,302
[Hiraku groans]

214
00:09:24,433 --> 00:09:25,477
This is really strong!

215
00:09:25,608 --> 00:09:27,088
[Donovan laughing]

216
00:09:27,218 --> 00:09:29,656
- I guess the mayor's
a bit of a lightweight.

217
00:09:29,786 --> 00:09:32,136
- Donovan and his men ended up
staying in the village

218
00:09:32,267 --> 00:09:34,399
and working as our brewers.

219
00:09:34,530 --> 00:09:36,358
Now that we've got new alcohol,

220
00:09:36,488 --> 00:09:38,099
it's time to have
a welcome party

221
00:09:38,229 --> 00:09:40,057
for the beastmen
and the dwarfs!

222
00:09:40,188 --> 00:09:41,755
Drink up, everyone!

223
00:09:41,885 --> 00:09:46,411
[all cheering]
[tavern music]

224
00:09:46,542 --> 00:09:48,675
- You can really taste
all the fragrance that went

225
00:09:48,805 --> 00:09:50,981
into this alcohol
when you give it a sip.

226
00:09:51,112 --> 00:09:54,376
- I really like this mayonnaise!

227
00:09:54,506 --> 00:09:56,160
- This goes perfect
with the booze.

228
00:09:56,291 --> 00:09:58,293
- Let's drink all night,
everyone!

229
00:09:58,423 --> 00:10:00,121
- He snuck in again.

230
00:10:00,251 --> 00:10:01,775
- I don't mind that
he comes here,

231
00:10:01,905 --> 00:10:03,994
but he always drinks
way too much of our wine.

232
00:10:04,125 --> 00:10:06,214
- Right, it's time to
show you all my special

233
00:10:06,344 --> 00:10:07,824
one-of-a-kind technique.

234
00:10:08,564 --> 00:10:09,957
[Dryme snoring]

235
00:10:10,087 --> 00:10:11,611
[Hiraku chuckling]

236
00:10:11,741 --> 00:10:13,613
- Thanks for everything, mayor.

237
00:10:13,743 --> 00:10:16,441
It was very kind of you
to take us all in.

238
00:10:16,572 --> 00:10:17,660
- Don't mention it.

239
00:10:17,791 --> 00:10:19,401
We're all happy you're here.

240
00:10:19,531 --> 00:10:20,750
- Yeah!

241
00:10:20,881 --> 00:10:21,838
There are a lot of people
in this village

242
00:10:21,969 --> 00:10:23,405
who like to drink.

243
00:10:24,145 --> 00:10:25,494
- Wait a minute,

244
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:28,671
I finally got some adult men
to join the village.

245
00:10:29,933 --> 00:10:31,108
By the way, Donovan,

246
00:10:31,239 --> 00:10:33,110
I'm not asking for any
particular reason,

247
00:10:33,241 --> 00:10:35,765
but are there any girls here
who catch your eye?

248
00:10:35,896 --> 00:10:37,637
You know, that kind that
make you think,

249
00:10:37,767 --> 00:10:39,247
"Wow, she's pretty!"

250
00:10:39,377 --> 00:10:42,554
- Well, I can certainly say
that they're all very

251
00:10:42,685 --> 00:10:44,382
good looking and all,
but you know,

252
00:10:44,513 --> 00:10:46,558
I think they're just a bit
too young for me.

253
00:10:46,689 --> 00:10:48,691
If they can't at least
grow a beard,

254
00:10:48,822 --> 00:10:51,302
then they're not for me.

255
00:10:51,433 --> 00:10:53,174
- [Hiraku] A beard?

256
00:10:53,304 --> 00:10:55,698
- Man, why are you making me
say it out loud like that?

257
00:10:55,829 --> 00:10:57,874
- The cultural barrier is high.

258
00:10:58,005 --> 00:10:58,919
[Hiraku hiccups]

259
00:10:59,049 --> 00:11:00,007
Farming Life...

260
00:11:00,137 --> 00:11:01,182
- [Senu] In Another...

261
00:11:01,312 --> 00:11:02,749
- [Hiraku] World.

262
00:11:05,621 --> 00:11:08,755
[dragon whooshing]
[horn blowing]

263
00:11:08,885 --> 00:11:11,671
[dramatic music]

264
00:11:15,587 --> 00:11:17,720
Don't tell me there's
another wyvern.

265
00:11:17,851 --> 00:11:19,679
Wait, a dragon?

266
00:11:19,809 --> 00:11:20,854
It's headed straight for us!

267
00:11:20,984 --> 00:11:23,160
It doesn't look friendly.

268
00:11:23,291 --> 00:11:24,771
I'm going to
finish this one off

269
00:11:24,901 --> 00:11:27,687
before it causes any
damage to the village.

270
00:11:28,339 --> 00:11:30,298
[dragon crashing]

271
00:11:30,428 --> 00:11:31,778
What just happened?

272
00:11:31,908 --> 00:11:33,605
Isn't that Dryme?

273
00:11:33,736 --> 00:11:35,738
Is this infighting?

274
00:11:35,869 --> 00:11:38,045
But they're just
staring each other down.

275
00:11:39,829 --> 00:11:40,874
There's another one!

276
00:11:41,004 --> 00:11:42,397
[dragon roaring]

277
00:11:42,527 --> 00:11:43,964
That one's dangerous.

278
00:11:44,094 --> 00:11:45,487
[Hiraku grunts]

279
00:11:46,793 --> 00:11:48,620
[spear whooshing]

280
00:11:48,751 --> 00:11:49,883
I missed!

281
00:11:50,013 --> 00:11:51,232
[spear zaps]

282
00:11:51,362 --> 00:11:53,190
But the next one won't.

283
00:11:53,321 --> 00:11:54,670
- Please, wait, mayor!

284
00:11:54,801 --> 00:11:57,717
That isn't an enemy
to the village!

285
00:11:57,847 --> 00:12:00,154
[Hiraku groans]

286
00:12:00,284 --> 00:12:02,809
I'm terribly sorry
for the confusion.

287
00:12:02,939 --> 00:12:05,028
These two are my
master's beloved wife

288
00:12:05,159 --> 00:12:06,900
and his precious daughter.

289
00:12:07,030 --> 00:12:08,597
- My name is Lastismoon.

290
00:12:08,728 --> 00:12:10,947
- I'm Graffaloon,
nice to meet you.

291
00:12:11,078 --> 00:12:12,079
- Nice to meet you.

292
00:12:12,209 --> 00:12:13,733
I'm Hiraku Machio.

293
00:12:13,863 --> 00:12:16,692
Why are your wife
and daughter here?

294
00:12:17,475 --> 00:12:19,129
- Well, you see.

295
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:21,697
- Apparently Dryme's constant
sneaking out so that he could

296
00:12:21,828 --> 00:12:25,527
come to our village has roused
some suspicion at home.

297
00:12:25,657 --> 00:12:27,790
- [Lastismoon] What were we
supposed to think when he was

298
00:12:27,921 --> 00:12:29,661
sneaking out every night?

299
00:12:29,792 --> 00:12:31,272
- [Graffaloon] If it turned out
he was sneaking out

300
00:12:31,402 --> 00:12:32,795
to do something he shouldn't.

301
00:12:32,926 --> 00:12:34,928
[Dryme laughing]

302
00:12:35,058 --> 00:12:37,495
- What an utterly
ridiculous accusation.

303
00:12:37,626 --> 00:12:39,541
- But you were sneaking off
with all kinds of stuff

304
00:12:39,671 --> 00:12:40,977
from the treasury.

305
00:12:41,108 --> 00:12:42,718
- And not coming home
till the morning.

306
00:12:42,849 --> 00:12:44,633
- Oh, I get it now.

307
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:46,896
It's the gifts he's
always bringing us.

308
00:12:47,027 --> 00:12:49,159
And I was worried about him
going home drunk,

309
00:12:49,290 --> 00:12:50,552
so I built him a house.

310
00:12:50,682 --> 00:12:52,423
Maybe that wasn't
such a good idea.

311
00:12:52,554 --> 00:12:55,339
- That was for the sake of
our diplomatic relations.

312
00:12:55,470 --> 00:12:57,559
It was all very high
level politics-

313
00:12:57,689 --> 00:12:59,082
- He's hiding something, mother.

314
00:12:59,213 --> 00:13:00,083
- Yes.

315
00:13:00,214 --> 00:13:01,389
At this point,

316
00:13:01,519 --> 00:13:04,740
my suspicions are
all being confirmed.

317
00:13:04,871 --> 00:13:05,828
- [Hiraku] She's scary.

318
00:13:05,959 --> 00:13:07,308
- Wait a minute, you two!

319
00:13:07,438 --> 00:13:08,875
Just think about it.

320
00:13:09,005 --> 00:13:11,051
Don't you think this man
actually has the courage

321
00:13:11,181 --> 00:13:13,531
to have an affair like that?!

322
00:13:13,662 --> 00:13:15,229
- That's a good point.
[chimes ringing]

323
00:13:15,359 --> 00:13:16,621
- Oh, thank goodness.

324
00:13:16,752 --> 00:13:18,145
- Are you all happy with that?

325
00:13:18,275 --> 00:13:19,711
Excuse me.

326
00:13:19,842 --> 00:13:21,409
Even though I don't know you,

327
00:13:21,539 --> 00:13:22,889
I'm sorry about earlier.

328
00:13:23,019 --> 00:13:24,760
- No, no, no!
Don't worry about it!

329
00:13:24,891 --> 00:13:26,240
This was all our fault.

330
00:13:26,370 --> 00:13:28,677
Come on, you two,
apologize to the mayor!

331
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:31,071
- I'm sorry I tried to
burn the village down

332
00:13:31,201 --> 00:13:33,247
because I thought my dad
was having an affair.

333
00:13:33,377 --> 00:13:35,510
- And I'm sorry that I was
about to obliterate

334
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:38,426
the insolent man who pointed
a spear at my dear daughter.

335
00:13:38,556 --> 00:13:39,949
- [Hiraku] They're scary!

336
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:42,169
- Well then, I guess
everything settled now.

337
00:13:42,299 --> 00:13:44,911
- But dear husband, you
still shouldn't sneak out

338
00:13:45,041 --> 00:13:46,303
to get drunk like that.

339
00:13:46,434 --> 00:13:47,957
- What are you saying?

340
00:13:48,088 --> 00:13:49,567
- [Lastismoon] She said,
you still shouldn't sneak out

341
00:13:49,698 --> 00:13:50,742
to get drunk like that.

342
00:13:50,873 --> 00:13:52,222
- Well, I'm just glad to see

343
00:13:52,353 --> 00:13:54,398
that they're getting along.

344
00:13:54,529 --> 00:13:55,922
Okay, see you all later.

345
00:13:56,052 --> 00:13:57,358
- Yes.

346
00:13:59,012 --> 00:14:00,840
Do you see what I was doing?

347
00:14:00,970 --> 00:14:03,320
- Yes.

348
00:14:03,451 --> 00:14:05,409
- Our continued relationship
with this village

349
00:14:05,540 --> 00:14:07,281
is of the utmost importance.

350
00:14:07,411 --> 00:14:08,935
- Despite their lack of numbers,

351
00:14:09,065 --> 00:14:11,938
they still possess the power
necessary to challenge us.

352
00:14:12,068 --> 00:14:13,809
I never thought
we'd meet anyone

353
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:15,898
that had the strength
to overwhelm us.

354
00:14:16,029 --> 00:14:17,334
- Yeah, you're right.

355
00:14:17,465 --> 00:14:18,988
You couldn't even defend
against that attack,

356
00:14:19,119 --> 00:14:21,121
you had to avoid it.

357
00:14:21,251 --> 00:14:23,645
- [Graffaloon] Even that was
only thanks to the spider.

358
00:14:23,775 --> 00:14:27,736
- [Lamulias] Spider?
- Yes, an old friend of mine.

359
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:29,651
Had I not been pulled
out of the way,

360
00:14:29,781 --> 00:14:32,219
I may not be standing
here with you now.

361
00:14:32,349 --> 00:14:33,524
Lasti.

362
00:14:33,655 --> 00:14:35,004
- Yes?

363
00:14:35,135 --> 00:14:38,268
- I have a very important
job for you to do.

364
00:14:38,399 --> 00:14:40,401
I want you to live here
for a while.

365
00:14:40,531 --> 00:14:41,271
- Oh!

366
00:14:41,402 --> 00:14:42,533
Mother, why?

367
00:14:42,664 --> 00:14:43,970
- Why would you do that?

368
00:14:44,100 --> 00:14:45,667
- This is a good chance
for you to be quiet.

369
00:14:45,797 --> 00:14:47,016
- Yes, dear.

370
00:14:47,147 --> 00:14:49,149
- We can't ignore
that kind of power.

371
00:14:49,279 --> 00:14:51,412
I don't expect you to be
able to suppress it.

372
00:14:51,542 --> 00:14:53,457
I just expect you
to do your duty

373
00:14:53,588 --> 00:14:56,156
and make sure that such power
is not turned on us.

374
00:14:56,286 --> 00:14:57,635
Is that understood?

375
00:14:57,766 --> 00:15:00,595
- Yes. I will do my best.

376
00:15:00,725 --> 00:15:02,118
- Is that wise?

377
00:15:02,249 --> 00:15:04,555
- Yes. I believe that
choosing this path

378
00:15:04,686 --> 00:15:06,862
will lead to the best
outcome for Lasti.

379
00:15:06,993 --> 00:15:08,864
I can feel it within me.

380
00:15:09,734 --> 00:15:10,910
- Sure.

381
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:12,694
I don't mind if she stays.

382
00:15:12,824 --> 00:15:14,914
- I look forward to
working here!

383
00:15:15,044 --> 00:15:17,568
If you wouldn't mind,
please call me Lasti.

384
00:15:17,699 --> 00:15:19,266
- Sure. Sounds good.

385
00:15:19,396 --> 00:15:21,659
- So then, what do you
want me to do?

386
00:15:21,790 --> 00:15:26,360
- And like that,
Lasti immediately went
to work in the village.

387
00:15:26,490 --> 00:15:28,144
- I'm ready to start now!

388
00:15:28,275 --> 00:15:30,712
- Uh, are you a dragon creature?

389
00:15:30,842 --> 00:15:32,627
- [Hiraku] However.
[tomato splats]

390
00:15:32,757 --> 00:15:34,455
[Senu whimpers]
- What the?

391
00:15:34,585 --> 00:15:37,371
[Lastismoon humming]

392
00:15:37,501 --> 00:15:39,939
- [Hiraku] Dragons are pretty
extraordinary in all regards.

393
00:15:40,069 --> 00:15:42,202
- Gently.

394
00:15:42,332 --> 00:15:43,725
Gently.

395
00:15:45,118 --> 00:15:46,554
[Lastismoon sneezes]

396
00:15:46,684 --> 00:15:49,426
[apples explodes]

397
00:15:50,732 --> 00:15:52,125
- [Hiraku] It looks like
it'll take a while

398
00:15:52,255 --> 00:15:54,040
for her to get used to her work.

399
00:15:54,170 --> 00:15:55,693
[boy laughing]

400
00:15:55,824 --> 00:15:57,086
- Wait up!

401
00:15:57,217 --> 00:15:59,132
- [Hiraku] What should we
do with her?

402
00:15:59,262 --> 00:16:00,829
- [Tia] You don't need to
make her do something

403
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,396
she isn't a fit for.

404
00:16:02,526 --> 00:16:04,572
- But Dryme really
wanted to give her

405
00:16:04,702 --> 00:16:07,053
some work to do
around here.

406
00:16:07,183 --> 00:16:08,968
[wolf whimpering]
What is it?

407
00:16:09,098 --> 00:16:10,926
- They've been acting like this
ever since the dragons

408
00:16:11,057 --> 00:16:12,580
showed up in the village.

409
00:16:12,710 --> 00:16:15,844
The cows and chickens have
been acting scared too.

410
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:18,020
We haven't been able to
get any milk or eggs.

411
00:16:18,151 --> 00:16:19,108
[Hiraku sighs]

412
00:16:19,239 --> 00:16:20,762
- Dryme acts like that,

413
00:16:20,892 --> 00:16:22,938
so I wasn't really
thinking about it,

414
00:16:23,069 --> 00:16:25,288
but everyone is normally
afraid of dragons, aren't they?

415
00:16:25,419 --> 00:16:28,161
- It's not just the power
they have either.

416
00:16:28,291 --> 00:16:31,164
Their knowledge and
wisdom is also great.

417
00:16:32,295 --> 00:16:33,905
- In that case.

418
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:38,649
- [Lastismoon] Sorry to
keep you waiting.

419
00:16:38,780 --> 00:16:40,477
- Don't worry about.
[Beezel grunting]

420
00:16:40,608 --> 00:16:42,218
- I'm Lastismoon,

421
00:16:42,349 --> 00:16:44,481
and I'm in charge of handling
diplomatic relations

422
00:16:44,612 --> 00:16:45,917
here at the village.

423
00:16:46,048 --> 00:16:48,746
- Don't tell me you are
that dragon girl.

424
00:16:48,877 --> 00:16:49,660
- I am.

425
00:16:49,791 --> 00:16:51,358
Please call me Lasti.

426
00:16:51,488 --> 00:16:54,404
What is it that you've come
to request from us today?

427
00:16:54,535 --> 00:16:55,884
[Beezel whimpers]

428
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,364
- We'd like to get
more of those

429
00:16:57,494 --> 00:16:58,887
bright colored fruit
we got last time.

430
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:00,628
- You mean the oranges, right?

431
00:17:00,758 --> 00:17:03,457
I'm sorry to say our stock
is running quite low.

432
00:17:03,587 --> 00:17:06,025
Could I interest you in
strawberries instead?

433
00:17:06,155 --> 00:17:07,678
They're perfectly ripe now.

434
00:17:07,809 --> 00:17:10,942
- In that case, I'll take
10 boxes of those, please.

435
00:17:11,073 --> 00:17:13,206
- Wow! Thank you so much!

436
00:17:13,336 --> 00:17:15,034
Could I interest you in
some apples and pears

437
00:17:15,164 --> 00:17:16,600
to go with them?

438
00:17:16,731 --> 00:17:18,863
We have persimmons
and watermelons too.

439
00:17:18,994 --> 00:17:22,128
- Okay, I'll take those.

440
00:17:22,258 --> 00:17:23,651
- [Lastismoon]
Here's your order.

441
00:17:23,781 --> 00:17:25,044
- Thank you very much.

442
00:17:25,174 --> 00:17:27,046
- Would you like to
count them to confirm?

443
00:17:27,176 --> 00:17:28,569
- That won't be necessary!

444
00:17:28,699 --> 00:17:29,874
- [Lastismoon]
Very well.

445
00:17:30,005 --> 00:17:31,267
We look forward to
seeing you again.

446
00:17:31,398 --> 00:17:33,487
- It looks like she's got
the hang of this.

447
00:17:33,617 --> 00:17:35,054
- What?!

448
00:17:35,184 --> 00:17:37,404
They have dragons now?!
This is a joke!

449
00:17:37,534 --> 00:17:40,668
- That village's military
might grows by the day.

450
00:17:40,798 --> 00:17:42,583
- We need to monitor them.

451
00:17:42,713 --> 00:17:44,759
Should we send a spy
there to the village?

452
00:17:44,889 --> 00:17:47,196
- If they find out,
it'll be an act of aggression!

453
00:17:47,327 --> 00:17:50,156
[Beezel sighs]
- We have no other choice.

454
00:17:50,286 --> 00:17:52,027
I have a plan.

455
00:17:52,158 --> 00:17:54,464
[door clicking]
- Pardon me, Father.

456
00:17:54,595 --> 00:17:56,727
I understand you called for me.

457
00:17:56,858 --> 00:17:57,902
- Yes.

458
00:17:58,033 --> 00:18:00,166
Flowrem, please have a seat.

459
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:03,473
- I see.

460
00:18:03,604 --> 00:18:06,172
You want me to investigate
that Great Tree Village?

461
00:18:06,302 --> 00:18:07,434
- Yes.

462
00:18:07,564 --> 00:18:09,566
In particular,
their military might.

463
00:18:09,697 --> 00:18:12,308
However, you mustn't do
anything rash.

464
00:18:12,439 --> 00:18:15,572
Your safety must always be
your number one concern.

465
00:18:15,703 --> 00:18:17,096
- Understood.

466
00:18:17,226 --> 00:18:20,534
But Father, I am
your daughter, after all.

467
00:18:20,664 --> 00:18:24,190
I'm confident in my magic,
so don't worry.

468
00:18:25,365 --> 00:18:27,149
[Beezel sighs]

469
00:18:28,194 --> 00:18:29,804
[Flowrem zipping]

470
00:18:29,934 --> 00:18:31,414
Oh.

471
00:18:31,545 --> 00:18:34,765
At a glance, this seems
like an ordinary village,

472
00:18:34,896 --> 00:18:37,507
but how did they develop a
village like this in the middle

473
00:18:37,638 --> 00:18:40,597
of a forest filled with such
terrifying monsters?

474
00:18:40,728 --> 00:18:43,034
- Welcome to the
Great Tree Village!

475
00:18:43,165 --> 00:18:46,037
I'm Lastismoon, head of
diplomatic relations.

476
00:18:46,168 --> 00:18:48,214
- It's nice to meet you.

477
00:18:48,344 --> 00:18:50,955
- You're going to stay here in
this village for a while, right?

478
00:18:51,086 --> 00:18:52,740
I heard from Beezel.

479
00:18:52,870 --> 00:18:54,350
You can call me Lasti.

480
00:18:54,481 --> 00:18:57,788
- Isn't Lastismoon
that infamous dragon

481
00:18:57,919 --> 00:18:59,964
that everyone is afraid of?

482
00:19:00,095 --> 00:19:03,316
I can't believe I've already
met someone this powerful.

483
00:19:04,839 --> 00:19:06,101
- Are you okay?

484
00:19:06,232 --> 00:19:07,189
I'm going to show you
around the village.

485
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:09,060
- Oh! Okay!

486
00:19:09,191 --> 00:19:11,367
- And this here
is our vineyard.

487
00:19:11,498 --> 00:19:14,196
We can make delicious wine
from these grapes here.

488
00:19:14,327 --> 00:19:16,329
My father said that
the wine here is the most-

489
00:19:16,459 --> 00:19:18,592
- It seems like just
an ordinary vineyard.

490
00:19:18,722 --> 00:19:20,333
- Roar!

491
00:19:20,463 --> 00:19:22,465
- [Flowrem] Why is a legendary
dragon in a place like this

492
00:19:22,596 --> 00:19:24,859
bragging to me about
crops they're growing?

493
00:19:24,989 --> 00:19:28,776
- And get this, so then
my dad told me that- Oh.

494
00:19:28,906 --> 00:19:30,517
- I'm sorry to interrupt.

495
00:19:30,647 --> 00:19:32,823
I've spotted a messenger
from Howling Village.

496
00:19:32,954 --> 00:19:34,651
- Oh! Okay, thank you!

497
00:19:34,782 --> 00:19:37,959
Sorry, I need to go and take
care of something for a second.

498
00:19:38,089 --> 00:19:39,439
- Don't you worry about it.

499
00:19:39,569 --> 00:19:41,005
I can look around on my own.

500
00:19:41,136 --> 00:19:42,877
- Okay. See you later.

501
00:19:43,921 --> 00:19:45,706
- This works out perfectly.

502
00:19:45,836 --> 00:19:48,926
I can take the opportunity to
analyze their military strength.

503
00:19:51,799 --> 00:19:53,844
Those are lizardmen.

504
00:19:53,975 --> 00:19:56,064
Beastmen and ogres.

505
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:58,022
And even dwarves.

506
00:19:58,153 --> 00:20:00,111
They'll all be
tough to deal with,

507
00:20:00,242 --> 00:20:01,765
but with the full force
of our military,

508
00:20:01,896 --> 00:20:04,812
we should be able
to handle them.

509
00:20:04,942 --> 00:20:06,553
This might be their
headquarters.

510
00:20:06,683 --> 00:20:08,685
The Vampire Princess!

511
00:20:08,816 --> 00:20:10,774
I heard she was on the run
from Nobles,

512
00:20:10,905 --> 00:20:12,123
so she was laying low.

513
00:20:12,254 --> 00:20:13,995
What's she doing here?

514
00:20:14,125 --> 00:20:16,998
The Angel of Annihilation, Tia.

515
00:20:17,128 --> 00:20:20,915
Why is she in the same
village as Lulucy ?

516
00:20:21,045 --> 00:20:23,265
And I'm pretty sure I heard
that those three are called

517
00:20:23,396 --> 00:20:25,572
the Trio of Killer Angels.

518
00:20:26,616 --> 00:20:28,488
They even have high elves here?

519
00:20:28,618 --> 00:20:30,794
I've heard that those
are terrifying man eaters

520
00:20:30,925 --> 00:20:34,145
that prey upon helpless
young men and kidnap them.

521
00:20:34,276 --> 00:20:35,756
If there are five here,

522
00:20:35,886 --> 00:20:38,759
then this is already
too much for our military.

523
00:20:38,889 --> 00:20:40,326
Impossible!

524
00:20:40,456 --> 00:20:42,806
And they have inferno wolves
and demon spiders,

525
00:20:42,937 --> 00:20:44,547
and they formed a pack?!

526
00:20:44,678 --> 00:20:47,420
Up until now, I've been proud to
call myself one of the most

527
00:20:47,550 --> 00:20:51,337
talented magic users in all of
the Demonic Kingdom, but

528
00:20:51,467 --> 00:20:54,035
I feel like all my confidence
has left me.

529
00:20:56,429 --> 00:20:58,474
To command all of these
powerful troops,

530
00:20:58,605 --> 00:21:01,042
it would make sense to
assume that Lastismoon

531
00:21:01,172 --> 00:21:03,566
was in charge of such
an organization.

532
00:21:03,697 --> 00:21:06,134
But there's someone above
her called the Mayor

533
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:08,702
who rules over all of them.

534
00:21:08,832 --> 00:21:12,271
What kind of terrifying
opponent am I dealing with?

535
00:21:12,401 --> 00:21:13,707
Huh?

536
00:21:14,490 --> 00:21:15,404
- Huh?

537
00:21:15,535 --> 00:21:17,450
- It's just a human?

538
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:20,453
Why is a human
here of all places?

539
00:21:20,583 --> 00:21:22,629
- What are you doing out here?

540
00:21:22,759 --> 00:21:24,848
Are you lost or something?

541
00:21:24,979 --> 00:21:26,676
- Don't worry about me.

542
00:21:26,807 --> 00:21:28,939
I'm not so weak that
I need an ordinary human

543
00:21:29,070 --> 00:21:30,811
to worry about me.

544
00:21:31,942 --> 00:21:34,249
What? That person
I saw just now?

545
00:21:34,380 --> 00:21:36,817
- Yep. That's the mayor
of our village.

546
00:21:36,947 --> 00:21:39,341
- But isn't he just
an ordinary human?

547
00:21:39,472 --> 00:21:42,301
- He's a human strong enough
to defeat my mom if he wants.

548
00:21:42,431 --> 00:21:43,737
- That just can't be!

549
00:21:43,867 --> 00:21:45,608
- [Lastismoon]
Did you say hello?

550
00:21:45,739 --> 00:21:49,133
- Forget saying hello,
I was outright rude to him.

551
00:21:50,613 --> 00:21:52,006
There we go.

552
00:21:52,136 --> 00:21:54,095
[bright music]

553
00:21:56,271 --> 00:21:58,621
- I found out that girl
was Beezel's daughter.

554
00:21:58,752 --> 00:22:01,537
Apparently she's going to
live here for a while.

555
00:22:01,668 --> 00:22:04,627
She seems to be getting
along well with Lasti.

556
00:22:04,758 --> 00:22:07,456
That's great and all, but...

557
00:22:07,587 --> 00:22:09,110
- Good morning, mayor!

558
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:10,416
- Good morning.

559
00:22:10,546 --> 00:22:12,548
- I hope you have
a lovely day.

560
00:22:12,679 --> 00:22:16,726
- For some reason she acted
like this for a while.

561
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:21,688
["Feel the winds"
by Yui Hizuki plays]

562
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:50,603
[rustic music playing]

